# Canonical graphical notation catalog

SWAML 1.1 Â· publication 1.1.1. This generated catalog defines the original monochrome notation for each authored concept and meaningful label group. All specimens derive from [the semantic inventory](../spec/notation.json); complete examples supply their validation context.

Each SVG, PNG and vector scene shares the same geometry. A graphical specimen is a projection of its textual model; it does not create additional ports, events, state owners or execution semantics. Labels such as QoS values and expression operators appear within their owning element rather than introducing independent nodes.

The following fragments are contextual notation samples, not standalone SWAML files. `def` identifies reusable component/unit types; a root is an occurrence selected for execution.

## Concept index

- [Assertion](#notation-assert) â€” Operation flow.
- [Assignment](#notation-assignment) â€” Operation flow.
- [Boundary delegation](#notation-delegation) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Bounded loop](#notation-bounded-loop) â€” Operation flow.
- [Browser](#notation-view-browser) â€” View projections.
- [Case](#notation-case) â€” Cases and evidence.
- [Case causal order](#notation-case-causal-order) â€” Cases and evidence.
- [Case data exchange](#notation-case-data-exchange) â€” Cases and evidence.
- [Case event exchange](#notation-case-event-exchange) â€” Cases and evidence.
- [Case request](#notation-case-request) â€” Cases and evidence.
- [Case View](#notation-view-cv) â€” View projections.
- [Clientâ€“server interface](#notation-client-server-interface) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Completion transition](#notation-completion-transition) â€” Operation states.
- [Component definition](#notation-component-definition) â€” Structure and values.
- [Component usage](#notation-component-usage) â€” Structure and values.
- [Concurrency mode](#notation-concurrency-mode) â€” Timing and deployment.
- [Conditional branch](#notation-conditional) â€” Operation flow.
- [Correlated case reply](#notation-case-reply) â€” Cases and evidence.
- [Data member](#notation-data-member) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Data receiver port](#notation-port-receiver) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Data send](#notation-send) â€” Operation flow.
- [Data sender port](#notation-port-sender) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Delivery policy](#notation-delivery-policy) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Deployment binding](#notation-deployment) â€” Timing and deployment.
- [Duration value](#notation-duration) â€” Timing and deployment.
- [Enumeration](#notation-enumeration) â€” Structure and values.
- [Enumeration value](#notation-enum-value) â€” Structure and values.
- [Event member](#notation-event-member) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Event publication](#notation-publish) â€” Operation flow.
- [Event publisher port](#notation-port-publisher) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Event subscriber port](#notation-port-subscriber) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Executable operation](#notation-operation) â€” Operation flow.
- [Execution node](#notation-execution-node) â€” Timing and deployment.
- [Expressions and value paths](#notation-expression) â€” Structure and values.
- [Failure](#notation-fail) â€” Operation flow.
- [Final state](#notation-final-state) â€” Operation states.
- [Fixed array type and value](#notation-array-value) â€” Structure and values.
- [Flow View](#notation-view-fv) â€” View projections.
- [General View](#notation-view-gv) â€” View projections.
- [Grid View](#notation-view-grv) â€” View projections.
- [Initial state reference](#notation-initial-state) â€” Operation states.
- [Inline root composition](#notation-inline-root) â€” Structure and values.
- [Interconnect View](#notation-view-iv) â€” View projections.
- [Interface connector](#notation-connector) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Interface operation signature](#notation-operation-signature) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Local declaration](#notation-local-declaration) â€” Operation flow.
- [Local operation invocation](#notation-invoke) â€” Operation flow.
- [Manual activation](#notation-trigger-manual) â€” Operation flow.
- [Message freshness bound](#notation-freshness-bound) â€” Interfaces and connections.
- [Occurrence lifeline](#notation-sequence-lifeline) â€” Cases and evidence.
